course: dictionary
lesson: 14475
title: Strong feelings in one word
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Passionate is an adjective. It describes a person, or something they say or do, that shows very strong feelings. Those feelings can be love, anger or excitement. It can also mean very keen on something.
explain: «Mia is passionate about drawing, and she sketches every single day.» Being passionate about drawing means she loves it so much that she wants to do it all the time. The sentence clues tell you that passionate means keen.
explain: «The speaker gave a passionate speech, and the whole hall cheered.» Here passionate shows strong feeling in the speech. Check your meaning by swapping in calm: «a calm speech, and the whole hall cheered» no longer fits the cheering, so passionate must mean full of feeling.
fact: Passionate is an adjective: passionate, more passionate, most passionate.
fact: «Passionate» means having or showing very strong feelings, such as love, anger or excitement.
fact: «Passionate» can also mean very keen on or interested in something, as in «passionate about football».
fact: Toad in the stories is passionate about each new craze: boats, then caravans, then motor cars.
fact: When you read a word like passionate, look for clues in the sentence, such as the feeling it describes or the thing the person is keen on.
exercise: «Sam is passionate about science.» What does passionate mean here? | Good at maths | Afraid of science | *Very keen on science | Bored of science
exercise: «The passionate speech made everyone cheer.» What does passionate suggest? | Quiet and calm | Lost and confused | *Strong feeling | Very tired
exercise: Which word means very keen on something? | lazy | *passionate | sleepy | empty
test: «The crowd was passionate in its support for the team.» What does passionate mean? | Walking slowly | Showing no feeling at all | Fast asleep | *Showing strong feeling
test: Which word is closest in meaning to passionate in «passionate about reading»? | quiet | *keen | sleepy | empty
exam: Which sentence shows a passionate person? | Tom sat quietly and read nothing at all. | Ben yawned and went to sleep. | *Ella cheered loudly and waved her flag, full of excitement for the match.
